//****************************************************************************
// WHAT SURVIVES DEATH, added 2026-08-29 at the shard owner's instruction:
// "some starter items stay on you even when you are dead".
//
// ITEMNEWBIE sets ATTR_NEWBIE (Source-X CChar.cpp:1206), and the death
// handler explicitly keeps those items -- CContainer.cpp:529, "keep newbie
// stuff". The mechanism was always there; this file simply never used it.
// Before today it held 262 ITEM= lines and NOT ONE ITEMNEWBIE=, so a new
// character lost absolutely everything on its first death.
//
// That is not a theoretical concern. Kaelen, this project's first warrior,
// died in the Britain graveyard and woke with no weapon, no food and no
// gold -- and could not recover, because buying food needs money and
// earning money needs a weapon. He then spent an entire 25-minute session
// failing the same errand (run_m5/r2b: goals=0/5, gold=0->0).
//
// THE LINE DRAWN, deliberately: clothing, the starting weapon or tool, and
// spellbooks survive -- losing those makes a character UNRECOVERABLE rather
// than merely poorer. GOLD, BANDAGES AND OTHER CONSUMABLES STILL DROP,
// because death has to cost something, and gold that survives death is a
// faucet by another name.
//
// STARTING GOLD IS 10,000, raised from 1,000 on 2026-08-29 at the owner's
// correction. Measured, not assumed: every character created before this
// reconciled as "gold persisted=0 server=1000". It stays droppable on
// death -- a bigger purse makes dying cost MORE, which is the point.
//****************************************************************************
//****************************************************************************
// SphereServer by: SphereServer development team and Menasoft.
// www.sphereserver.net
//****************************************************************************
VERSION=X1

[COMMENT sphere_newb]
Newbie templates are item templates used to create all the
starting stuff on the account based on which profession/skills
the player choose on character creation menu.

Default MALE_DEFAULT / FEMALE_DEFAULT templates are always used
no matter what the player choose. Useful to set default starting
items common to all templates.

Each profession/skill template can have optional
variants to human, elf and gargoyle races. Example:
  [NEWBIE Alchemy]
  [NEWBIE Alchemy Elf]
  [NEWBIE Alchemy Garg]

If the player choose an race which has no template set, the
default human template will be used by default.


